1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,859
An n8n workflow can pass a test,

2
00:00:02,919 --> 00:00:06,291
fail on real input, and fail again next
week

3
00:00:06,351 --> 00:00:07,817
for the same reason.

4
00:00:07,877 --> 00:00:10,105
Seeing the red node is easy.

5
00:00:10,165 --> 00:00:14,299
Proving the cause and keeping it out is
the reliability problem.

6
00:00:14,909 --> 00:00:19,875
Pisama closes the loop in six stages:
design controls, run,

7
00:00:19,935 --> 00:00:24,901
retain evidence, diagnose, verify the next
build, then prevent recurrence.

8
00:00:25,511 --> 00:00:29,979
The release harness begins with nineteen
source-backed n8n executions:

9
00:00:30,039 --> 00:00:34,508
healthy runs and known failures labeled
from their records.

10
00:00:34,568 --> 00:00:37,024
Eighteen form the regression set;

11
00:00:37,084 --> 00:00:39,539
one holdout is sealed separately.

12
00:00:39,599 --> 00:00:41,552
I run the workflow.

13
00:00:41,612 --> 00:00:46,584
Pisama evaluates each trace and retains a
stable case identity.

14
00:00:47,194 --> 00:00:49,282
Now we have evidence.

15
00:00:49,342 --> 00:00:55,189
This execution reached the consumer
without body dot required dot value,

16
00:00:55,249 --> 00:00:58,410
and n8n recorded the failed expression.

17
00:00:58,470 --> 00:01:02,706
Pisama retains the workflow, node, trace,
expected label,

18
00:01:02,766 --> 00:01:06,465
and detected result in one auditable
record.

19
00:01:07,075 --> 00:01:11,477
Pisama identifies a data-contract mismatch
and the missing path.

20
00:01:11,537 --> 00:01:16,435
A second case shows sixty-four seconds
against a thirty-second limit.

21
00:01:16,495 --> 00:01:20,897
The operator reviews the evidence before
any control changes.

22
00:01:20,957 --> 00:01:22,880
Diagnosis informs the decision.

23
00:01:22,940 --> 00:01:26,350
It does not silently rewrite the workflow.

24
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:31,385
The next build runs against the reviewed
corpus.

25
00:01:31,445 --> 00:01:34,188
Eighteen regression cases execute
asynchronously;

26
00:01:34,248 --> 00:01:36,431
the holdout remains excluded.

27
00:01:36,491 --> 00:01:39,234
Every expected failure set matched,

28
00:01:39,294 --> 00:01:44,280
with the build revision and each case
result stored.

29
00:01:44,340 --> 00:01:46,522
Label corrections append evidence.

30
00:01:46,582 --> 00:01:48,765
Earlier scores remain unchanged.

31
00:01:49,375 --> 00:01:54,370
For the contract failure, Pisama proposes
a deterministic input guard.

32
00:01:54,430 --> 00:01:59,426
Apply remains blocked until the operator
selects a rejection path.

33
00:01:59,486 --> 00:02:01,954
Two real requests test it.

34
00:02:02,014 --> 00:02:04,987
Malformed input stops before the consumer.

35
00:02:05,047 --> 00:02:06,504
Valid input passes.

36
00:02:06,564 --> 00:02:10,548
Pisama retains both results and the
rollback record.

37
00:02:11,158 --> 00:02:16,444
The chain now connects failure evidence to
a reviewed diagnosis,

38
00:02:16,504 --> 00:02:20,186
an auditable release, and a preventive
control.

39
00:02:20,246 --> 00:02:23,394
For teams operating critical n8n
workflows,

40
00:02:23,454 --> 00:02:25,533
incidents become reusable safeguards.

41
00:02:25,593 --> 00:02:27,137
See what failed.

42
00:02:27,197 --> 00:02:28,740
Prove the fix.

43
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:29,810
Prevent recurrence.

44
00:02:29,870 --> 00:02:31,414
Pisama dot ai.
